{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"start\">\n  <state id=\"start\">\n    <onentry>\n      <raise event=\"\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <invoke id=\"\" src=\"child.scxml\"/>\n  </state>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml082-names-over-name-bound.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":2,"notes":0,"total":2,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml082-names-over-name-bound.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":1046,"endLine":4,"startColumn":21,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<raise>` event name `exxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 an event name may have\n\n**Note:** every build bounds an event name to 1,024 bytes of UTF-8, so this `<raise>` could never run as written; SCXML 1.0 sets no length, and this is the implementation's bound (spec errata L.6)\n\n**Help:** shorten the `event` value to at most 1,024 bytes\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §4.2 <raise>","text":"`<raise>` event name `exxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 an event name may have"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":1158,"start":133},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML082"},{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml082-names-over-name-bound.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":1030,"endLine":6,"startColumn":17,"startLine":6}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<invoke>` ID `ixxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,013 bytes, so the `done.invoke.` event it raises is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 an event name may have\n\n**Note:** SCXML 1.0 §6.4: a finished invoked service \"MUST return a special event 'done.invoke.id' to the external event queue of the invoking process, where id is the invokeid for this invocation\"; every build bounds an event name to 1,024 bytes of UTF-8, so this invocation could never report that it finished; SCXML 1.0 sets no length, and this is the implementation's bound (spec errata L.6)\n\n**Help:** shorten the ID to at most 1,012 bytes\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>","text":"`<invoke>` ID `ixxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,013 bytes, so the `done.invoke.` event it raises is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 an event name may have"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":2206,"start":1193},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML082"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"every build bounds an event name, a `<send>` ID, and an `<invoke>` ID to 1,024 bytes of UTF-8 (the processor's interface bound), so a `<raise event>`, `<send event>`, `<send id>`, or `<invoke id>` written longer could never run as written. An `<invoke>` ID must also leave room for the `done.invoke.<ID>` event the invocation returns (SCXML 1.0 §6.4: the service \"MUST return a special event 'done.invoke.id'\"), 12 more bytes, so it may have at most 1,012. Lengths are of the value with its white space collapsed (XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), as the compiler reads it. Names computed at run time (`eventexpr`, generated IDs) that exceed the bound raise `error.execution` instead (SCXML 1.0 §3.12.2). SCXML 1.0 sets no length; this is the implementation's bound, listed in the specification errata (L.6), and it applies to every build"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: shorten the name to at most 1,024 bytes (1,012 for an `<invoke>` ID).\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML082` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#invoke","id":"SCXML082","name":"SCXML082","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an event name or a send or invoke ID is longer than a name may be"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}